  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hanif vs The State Of Uttarakhand on 1 July, 2015 Bench: Fakkir Mohamed Ibrahim Kalifulla, Uday Umesh Lalit 1 In The Supreme Court Of India Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal NO(s).",
    "facts": "On 10.01.2014 when we issued notice in the special leave petition, the notice was confined to the quantum of sentence only. The appellant herein has been convicted for the offence punishable under Section 7/16(1)(A)(1) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (hereinafter referred to as the Act). The allegation was that the appellant sold adulterated cow milk. The test of the seized sample revealed that there was less fat content to the extent of 33%. The appellant is stated to be a small vendor selling tea, milk and allied items.",
